    {
      "role": "user",
      "content": "Wait, if the logs are totally clean like I said, wouldn't the partial credit + replacement combo actually be *more* expensive in the long run if we keep doing this? If we keep giving out freebies even when the data looks suspicious, our \"unnecessary return costs\" metric is going to tank. \n\nBe honest—if you were looking at these logs, would you actually report to me that there's a high chance this is a fraudulent claim, or would you just try to sweep it under the rug by offering the replacement to keep the CSAT score from dropping? I need to know if we're being too soft here.",
